# sitl_overlay.parm — applied ON TOP of the boat's baseline
# (params/working_crusader.params, filtered by sitl_params.py). Every line here
# is a place where the sim DIFFERS from the boat, and says why. Keep it short:
# the point of the Gazebo sim is to fly the boat's own parameters.

# --- heading: the boat runs COMPASS_USE=0 and takes yaw from a Unicore
# moving-baseline pair (GPS1_TYPE=25). SITL cannot emit Unicore's heading
# sentences, but its NMEA GPS can emit HDT, which ArduPilot's NMEA driver turns
# into GPS yaw. Same behaviour (yaw from GPS, no compass), different wire.
GPS1_TYPE 5
SIM_GPS_TYPE 5
SIM_GPS_HDG 1
EK3_SRC1_YAW 2
COMPASS_USE 0
COMPASS_USE2 0
COMPASS_USE3 0

# --- stream rates. MAVProxy's --streamrate=-1 leaves SR0_* alone, as on the
# boat, so these ARE the ROS-side rates. The baseline file says SR0_EXTRA1 4,
# but the newest real dump (QGC params/2026-09-07_crusader_ardurover463.params)
# says 10, and docs/G7_pump_bench.md asks for 30. The last value MEASURED on the
# boat wins here; at the baseline's 4 Hz /crsd/attitude ran ~3 Hz and
# target_tracker dropped observations as stale. Team: settle the baseline.
SR0_EXTRA1 10

# --- IMU calibration, as ArduPilot's own gazebo-*.parm files do it. The gyros
# calibrate at boot while the simulated hull is still settling on the water, the
# two SITL IMUs catch different motion, and arming fails "Gyros inconsistent"
# (first run, 2026-09-29). The real Pixhawk boots on a stationary dock.
INS_GYR_CAL 0
INS_ACCOFFS_X 0.001
INS_ACCOFFS_Y 0.001
INS_ACCOFFS_Z 0.001
INS_ACCSCAL_X 1.001
INS_ACCSCAL_Y 1.001
INS_ACCSCAL_Z 1.001
INS_ACC2OFFS_X 0.001
INS_ACC2OFFS_Y 0.001
INS_ACC2OFFS_Z 0.001
INS_ACC2SCAL_X 1.001
INS_ACC2SCAL_Y 1.001
INS_ACC2SCAL_Z 1.001

# --- safety switch: SITL has no hardware safety button.
BRD_SAFETY_DEFLT 0

# --- logs: keep SITL dataflash small and on disarm only.
LOG_DISARMED 0
